{
  "schema": "experiment_ledger.v1",
  "_comment": [
    "Every `registration.<key>` boolean toggle read through `registration.flags.registration_flag`",
    "or `auth_flow.steps._registration_flag`, with the decision attached to it.",
    "",
    "Why: these toggles are the registration lane's experiment surface. Before this file the only",
    "record was the prose table in docs/current/registration-ab-runbook.md, which nothing verified,",
    "so a switch could be added without a hypothesis and removed without a verdict.",
    "",
    "kind: ab      -- a controlled comparison, identified by its runbook id (P0-1 ... P3-1).",
    "kind: feature -- a product switch, not an experiment; no runbook id, no expiry.",
    "",
    "status: open       -- awaiting a decision; uses its own `expires`, else the ledger-wide",
    "                      `review_date`. An expired entry means 'decide or retire'.",
    "        concluded  -- REQUIRES verdict; if the key is still read, REQUIRES keep.reason.",
    "        retired    -- the key must no longer be read by code.",
    "",
    "`review_date` is a batch review date. All open entries share it on purpose: the backlog is",
    "reviewed together twice a year, and a per-switch date nobody measured would be invented.",
    "String-valued switches (registration.preflight_login_page) are out of scope here: they are",
    "not read through the boolean flag helpers, so this file could not prove anything about them."
  ],
  "review_date": "2027-01-31",
  "dynamic_call_sites": [
    {
      "file": "sms_tool/registration/warmup.py",
      "function": "_leaf_flag",
      "reason": "reads registration.chatgpt_bootstrap.<key> one level deeper; enabled/authenticated are a feature pair, not registration.<key> toggles"
    }
  ],
  "toggles": {
